# MC-X-F2, a later base replace. L §6.4 as in L6_4_replace_entry_same_known: the scenario's replace (known 2027-01-01)
# stands in leave over the base's own replace known later (v3, 2027-06-01, lifespan to 2028-12-31), "whatever the two
# rows' known dates": the base counts beta_job on 2028-06-01 (v3), leave doesn't.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2027-07-01
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2028-12-31
source s "s"
kind jobs
version v1
  cite s
  known 2027-01-01
  jobs + [beta_job] lives 2027-08-01..
version v3
  cite s
  known 2027-06-01
  replace jobs + [beta_job] lives 2027-08-01..2028-12-31
ask n: count(j in jobs on 2028-06-01)
=== s.tally
scenario leave over m
  tally 2
  from 2028-03-01
version v2
  cite s
  known 2027-01-01
  replace jobs + [beta_job] lives 2027-08-01..2028-02-29
ask n2: count(j in jobs on 2028-06-01) in leave
=== expect
n: 1
  cut 2027-07-01
n2: 0
  world: leave
  cut 2027-07-01
